"""Rule catalogue: one entry per finding id, used by the SARIF reporter and to generate docs/checks.md.

Each rule has a name, a category, a default severity and a one-sentence description (used in SARIF),
plus the documentation fields: ``levels`` (every severity the scanner can report it at), ``trigger`` (what
makes it fire, Markdown) and, for some groups, ``why`` (why it matters, Markdown). After changing a rule, run
``python scripts/gen_checks_doc.py`` to refresh docs/checks.md; CI fails when the file is stale.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

